The  driver  provides support for IBM RT PC boards that multiplex
together up to four or communications interfaces.  Each device is
the master device for up to four devices.  The kernel  configura‐
tion  specifies  these devices as slave devices of the device, as
shown in the synopsis.  The specification for the device is  used
to compute the base addresses for the subdevices.  The driver was
written  by  Charles  Hannum, based on the driver.  The driver is
unlikely to work on non‐EISA and non‐PCI machines.  The  ISA  bus
only  asserts 10 I/O address lines, and this is not enough.  Even
on EISA and PCI machines, some address conflicts  have  been  ob‐
served.   On  one machine, the second port always conflicted with
something (though it’s not clear what)  and  caused  strange  re‐
sults.   Disabling  the  second port in the kernel config allowed
the other three ports to function correctly.
